| 8 | R-35 |', 11, '["GHBC-C-003164","GHBC-C-003165","GHBC-C-003166","GHBC-C-003167","GHBC-C-003168","GHBC-C-003169","GHBC-C-003170","GHBC-C-003171","GHBC-C-003172","GHBC-C-003173","GHBC-C-003174","GHBC-C-003175","GHBC-C-003176","GHBC-C-003177","GHBC-C-003178","GHBC-C-003179","GHBC-C-003180","GHBC-C-003181"]', '[588,589,590,591,592]', 10);
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO academy_lessons (id, course_id, slug, title, body_md, est_minutes, source_clauses_json, source_pages_json, sort_order) VALUES ('lesson-0e90b36191b83b7b', 'course-89312c0cbfae75d4', 'pro-009-l12', 'TEMPERATURE CONTROL', '### 13.10.1 Equipment and systems

Interior spaces intended for human occupancy shall be provided with active or passive space heating systems capable of maintaining an indoor temperature of not less than 68°F (20°C) at a point 914 mm (3 feet) above the floor on the design heating day.

Exceptions: Space heating systems are not required for:

1. Interior spaces where the primary purpose of the space is not associated with human comfort.

2. Group F, H, S or U occupancies.', 5, '["GHBC-C-003182"]', '[592]', 11);
